 de la Enfermedad Mórbida is a society that collaborates with SEEDO to establish guidelines for metabolic surgery.", "KUMPF:Kumpf is a researcher whose work reflects the outcomes of patients after metabolic surgery, particularly regarding dietary changes and complications.", "DOBRATZ:Dobratz is a researcher who evaluated predictive equations for measuring basal metabolic expenditure in obese women.", "CIRUGÍA METABÓLICA:Metabolic surgery is a medical procedure recommended for treating type 2 diabetes in patients with obesity.", "SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL:SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL refers to the provision of dietary assistance to patients who are unable to meet their nutritional needs through normal eating. This type of nutritional support is particularly crucial for patients who have undergone metabolic surgery, especially in cases where complications arise. It serves as a necessary intervention to ensure that these patients receive adequate nutrition during their recovery process.", "NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL:NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL, or parenteral nutrition (NP), is a medical treatment that provides essential nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the gastrointestinal tract. This method is utilized primarily in patients who are unable to consume food orally or tolerate enteral nutrition, particularly in cases such as pancreatitis or post-surgery recovery. During hospitalization, parenteral nutrition serves as an alternative means of nutritional support, ensuring that patients receive adequate nourishment when traditional feeding methods are not viable or contraindicated. Overall, NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL is a critical intervention for maintaining the nutritional status of patients who cannot meet their dietary needs through oral or enteral means.", "FUGA ANASTOMÓTICA:Fuga anastomótica is a common complication after metabolic surgery that may require nutritional support due to its impact on oral intake.", "NAÚSEAS Y VÓMITOS:Nauseas y vómitos are common post-operative complications that can limit a patient's ability to eat normally after metabolic surgery.", "MALABSORCIÓN SEVERA:Malabsorción severa is a serious condition that can occur post-surgery, affecting nutrient absorption and necessitating nutritional support.", "DIETA ORAL:Dieta oral refers to the normal diet that most patients transition to after metabolic surgery, although some may face complications that prevent this.", "CALORIMETRÍA INDIRECTA:Calorimetría indirecta is a method used to measure basal metabolic rate, which is important for determining nutritional needs in post-operative patients.", "EQUACIONES PREDICTIVAS:Ecuaciones predictivas are formulas used to estimate metabolic expenditure in patients, especially when calorimetry is unavailable.)<|COMPLETE|>"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}